# Example layouts for herdr-layout.
#
# To use one, copy its lines into a file named .herdr-layout at the root of your project
# and remove the leading "# ". Example 1 is left active, so this file works as-is.
#
# Columns: split  of  ratio  command   (write - for the default)


# 1. Claude, a shell below it, lazygit on the right
#
#    ┌──────────┬──────────┐
#    │  claude  │          │
#    ├──────────┤ lazygit  │
#    │  shell   │          │
#    └──────────┴──────────┘

-      -  -  claude
right  0  -  lazygit
down   0  -  -


# 2. Editor on top keeping 70%, a shell at the bottom
#
#    ┌─────────────────────┐
#    │        nvim         │
#    ├─────────────────────┤
#    │        shell        │
#    └─────────────────────┘
#
# -     -  -    nvim
# down  0  0.7  -


# 3. Install dependencies first, then Claude next to a dev server and a test watcher
#
#    ┌────────────┬────────┐
#    │            │  dev   │
#    │   claude   ├────────┤
#    │            │ tests  │
#    └────────────┴────────┘
#
# run    npm install
# -      -  -    claude
# right  0  0.6  npm run dev
# down   1  -    npm test -- --watch


# 4. Two agents side by side, lazygit across the bottom
#
#    ┌──────────┬──────────┐
#    │  claude  │  codex   │
#    ├──────────┴──────────┤
#    │       lazygit       │
#    └─────────────────────┘
#
# -      -  -    claude
# down   0  0.7  lazygit
# right  0  -    codex
